# Architecture lock

Follow the approved architecture. Do not replace it with a different design.

## Pipeline

- CSV and eSIGMA are the two input methods.
- Both must converge into the same normalized representation.
- Normalized data becomes Parquet.
- Parquet enters the Survey Data Intelligence Retrieval Layer (SIRL).
- SIRL is RAG-inspired structured-data intelligence, NOT traditional document RAG.
- SIRL creates dataset, variable, record, enumerator, cluster, district and historical profiles.
- Profiles are stored in SQLite.
- Unified Validation consumes those profiles.
- Unified Validation consists of Rules + Statistics + ML.
- Evidence is fused into a risk score.
- AI is optional enrichment/context/explanation.
- AI must never be the sole source of truth.
- Never send the complete Parquet dataset to an LLM.
- AI providers must use an abstraction layer and environment variables.
- The deterministic pipeline must work when AI is unavailable.

## Scope and stack

- Do not introduce Redis, Kafka, Celery, Kubernetes, PostgreSQL, vector databases, LangChain, LlamaIndex, or unnecessary infrastructure.
- Keep the architecture hackathon-scale.
- Python FastAPI backend, SQLite for metadata/results, Parquet for analytical data.
- Pandas, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, and PyArrow do deterministic processing.
- Frontend is Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind, Recharts, and Lucide React.

## Build order

Build bottom-up. Do not implement later phases until they are requested. Deterministic ingestion, profiling, and validation must work without any AI provider.
